From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:04:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ui): protect default scroll modes and reuse library
 preference collectors

Shared policy and Compose regression with Mihon 0084. User confirms category swipes improved, but filtering/switching to compact mode followed by folding still stutters. Regular native lists/grids/timeline/ScrollState paths bypassed the existing per-fling frame-time protection; apply the existing guard to every default Compose scroll entry in app and shared UI, preserving native velocity, bounds, consumption and cancellation. Wrap the wheel picker native snap without changing its snapping policy. Keep preview-only scrollbar examples unchanged and preserve Anikku-specific irregular grids. Cache the three library display/orientation PreferenceMutableState values for the model lifetime instead of starting model-scoped collectors on every getter call. Include density and layout direction in the scrollbar padding cache. Cover native scrolling through filter shrink, viewport changes, reverse fling, empty/short content and restoration, plus repeated timestamp and delegation behavior. Existing frame-clock algorithm, paging, layout, glass and decode behavior remain unchanged. No quantitative device FPS gain is claimed.
